/-
# Groups acting freely on abelian groups and skew-fields (Kourovka Notebook Problem 16.54)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 16.54 (V. D. Mazurov): we say that a group
`G` acts freely on a group `V` if `vg ≠ v` for any nontrivial `g ∈ G`, `v ∈ V`. Is it true that a
group `G` that can act freely on a non-trivial abelian group is embeddable in the multiplicative
group of some skew-field?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Defs
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Units.Defs
public import Mathlib.Algebra.GroupWithZero.Action.Defs

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.FreeActionSkewFieldEmbeddingKourovka16Problem54Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 16.54 (V. D.
Mazurov). UnsolvedMath record UM-00701246 (`KOU-16.54`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

Actions are by automorphisms (`DistribMulAction`, written on the left); a skew-field is a division
ring and embeddable means an injective homomorphism into its group of units. Groups, modules and
division rings are in `Type` (a division ring containing a copy of `G` contains one generated by it,
of cardinality at most `max(|G|, ℵ₀)`).
-/

/-- Kourovka 16.54 (V. D. Mazurov): a group `G` that acts freely by automorphisms on a nontrivial
abelian group `V` (`g • v ≠ v` for all `g ≠ 1` and `v ≠ 0`) embeds in the multiplicative group of
a division ring. -/
def freeActionEmbedsInSkewField : Prop :=
  ∀ (G : Type) [Group G],
    (∃ (V : Type) (_ : AddCommGroup V) (_ : Nontrivial V) (_ : DistribMulAction G V),
      ∀ g : G, g ≠ 1 → ∀ v : V, v ≠ 0 → g • v ≠ v) →
    ∃ (D : Type) (_ : DivisionRing D) (f : G →* Dˣ), Function.Injective f

/--
Resolved false: the Kourovka Archive answers 16.54 "No, it is not" (Nedrenko): the group `2.A₅.2`
with a quaternion Sylow 2-subgroup acts freely on an elementary abelian group of order `7⁴`, but by
Theorem 7 of Amitsur's classification of finite subgroups of division rings it does not embed in the
multiplicative group of any skew-field. Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved
Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of
Solved Problems, Problem 16.54 (V. D. Mazurov); resolution: D. Nedrenko, letter of 20 January 2014,
as recorded in the Kourovka Archive; S. A. Amitsur, Finite subgroups of division rings, Trans. Amer.
Math. Soc. 80 (1955), 361-386, Kourovka Archive, Problem 16.54 (No: 2.A_5.2 with a quaternion Sylow
2-subgroup acts freely on an elementary abelian group of order 7^4 but does not embed in the
multiplicative group of a skew-field, by Amitsur's Theorem 7).
-/
public theorem_wanted freeActionEmbedsInSkewField_refuted : ¬ freeActionEmbedsInSkewField

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.FreeActionSkewFieldEmbeddingKourovka16Problem54Wanted
